From 9276c810f10094fa184d647cfdd8e49098e829dd Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: William Floyd <git@notmy.space>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 22:21:57 +0000
Subject: ipa: soft: Select the chroma, tone curve, DRC tone mapping and lens
 shading by lux index

Each of the vendor tuning's cv12, gamma15, tmc12 and lsc3x has its own lux
index regions, as cc13 has, and the soft IPA used the one, for every light.
Adjust takes chromaLux, toneCurveLux and drcCurveLux, and Lsc luxSets, one
list of regions each, and blends the two regions either side of a gap in
their ranges with the lux index Agc estimates. The tone lookup table is
built again once the lux index moves by 5. Without the keys, or without
the lux model, the plain ones apply as before.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
